      <encodingDesc>
         <appInfo>
            <application>
               <name>musiconn.scoresearch</name>
               <p>Source OMR data.</p>
            </application>
            <application startdate="2025-08-29T17:35:12" enddate="2025-08-29T17:35:14" version="5.5.0-e003172">
               <name>Verovio</name>
               <p>Transcoded the OMR data from MusicXML to MEI for BSB images 00063-00091.</p>
            </application>
            <application startdate="2026-07-16T17:20:39" enddate="2026-08-16T16:56:32" version="1.4.2">
               <name>mei-friend</name>
               <p>Manual correction of the page files. The start is the earliest and the end the latest recorded in the page files for BSB images 00063-00091; 00068 and 00069 carry no record, and the second pass over 00063-00067 on 2026-10-25 is not recorded there.</p>
            </application>
         </appInfo>
         <editorialDecl>
            <p>This is a working digital edition based on DdT 1907, assembled on 2026-10-27 from the page-level encodings of BSB images 00063-00091 (printed pp. 33-61) at repository revision bad19e3. OMR and conversion errors are corrected against the DdT facsimile. Jingyu Tu corrected the page files from 2026-07-16 to 2026-10-25. Work-level correction has not started. No other witness has been consulted. Substantive departures from DdT are documented in editorial annotations recording the source reading, encoded reading, evidence or conjectural reasoning, and responsible editor; none has been recorded yet.</p>
            <p>The staff arrangement printed in DdT is retained: staff 1 is the flute (Flauto), staves 2 and 3 Violino I and II, staff 4 Viola, staff 5 Violoncello e Basso, and staves 6-7 and 8-9 the upper and lower staves of Cembalo I and Cembalo II. The cembalo staves as printed in DdT are retained as part of that edition. Who realized the figured bass in those staves is not established. They must be selected explicitly when defining an analytical view.</p>
            <p>Original page and system boundaries are represented by pb and sb elements. Surface and page-break numbers form a work-local sequence beginning with 1; the printed page range is recorded in sourceDesc. Each measure points to a measure zone on the corresponding facsimile surface using @facs. The 421 measures are numbered continuously across the 29 surfaces and the three movements: Allegro non molto (mm. 1-115), Largo e moderato (mm. 116-211) and Allegro (mm. 212-421).</p>
            <p>Editorial decisions that interpret or depart from the print are recorded as editorial annotations (annot type="editorial" with a CAMAT label) that point to the affected events.</p>
         </editorialDecl>
         <projectDesc>
            <p>This edition was prepared by CAMAT Corpus Editions as part of a DFG-funded corpus for music-analysis technologies (grant PF 669/18-1).</p>
         </projectDesc>
      </encodingDesc>
      <workList>
         <work xml:id="work.hasse_flute_concerto">
            <title>Konzert für Flöte, zwei Violinen, Viola und Bass</title>
            <composer>
               <persName auth="GND" auth.uri="https://d-nb.info/gnd/118546651" codedval="118546651">Johann Adolf Hasse</persName>
            </composer>
            <key pname="d" mode="major">D major</key>
            <perfMedium>
               <perfResList>
                  <perfRes solo="true">Flute</perfRes>
                  <perfRes>Violin I</perfRes>
                  <perfRes>Violin II</perfRes>
                  <perfRes>Viola</perfRes>
                  <perfRes>Violoncello and bass</perfRes>
                  <perfRes count="2">Harpsichord</perfRes>
               </perfResList>
            </perfMedium>
         </work>
      </workList>
      <revisionDesc>
         <change isodate="2026-10-27" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>Removed metcon="false" from the 30 measures that still carried it, inherited from the page files: every layer of each measure fills its meter and each measure contains every declared staff, so the CAMAT consistency check reports the same findings with and without the flags.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-27" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>Resolved the rhythm, layer and ID warnings of the CAMAT consistency check against the DdT facsimile. The 25 warnings were compared with the DdT page images by an AI model (OpenAI Codex); the editor spot-checked its readings in the page images and the MEI and approved the changes. Changed the last two chords of the beamed group in m. 307, staff 8, from quarters to the printed eighths (bdgrhy, ntgyuju); added the printed eighth rest after the quarter chord in m. 409, staff 6; renumbered the stem-down voice gbrhtyhy in m. 358, staff 8, from layer 1 to 2; padded the printed lower voice of m. 201, staff 8, which ends after two beats while the upper voice carries the third, with a quarter space; renumbered 16 single layers from 5 to 1 (mm. 54, 55, 62, 70, 126, 139, 140, 150, 181, 253, 307, 318, 319, 320, 348); and gave the leading space of m. 112, staff 8, layer 2 its xml:id aduchb, which the page file had typed as xml:base. The five Verovio mixed-beam warnings (mm. 22, 85, 105, 111) concern kneed beams that are printed as encoded and are left.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-27" resp="#resp.camat #resp.polyakov">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>Combined the page-level files for BSB images 00063-00091 into work-level MEI: one mdiv, 421 measures in three movements and 29 facsimile surfaces with measure zones (repository revision bad19e3). Measures and their zones are numbered continuously. The second system of 24 pages, encoded in the page files with a second pb, begins with an sb. The page-opening score definitions are not carried over except at printed p. 44 (m. 116, Largo e moderato), where the key of one sharp and the 3/4 meter are kept with page-qualified IDs (pg44_). 362 IDs that repeat an ID of an earlier page take page-qualified IDs (pg34_ to pg61_), and the references on their page follow. Gave the file the edition header of the MEI 5.1 CMN publication profile (work title, GND-linked composer, responsibilities, CC BY 4.0 data licence, DdT 1907 source with its BSB identifiers and printed pp. 33-61, application history, editorial declaration and principal work), linked the mdiv to the work and declared the mei-CMN schema with meiversion 5.1+CMN. No edition number is set until a release includes this work. The MusicXML-derived @ppq and @dur.ppq are dropped, as in the Pisendel and DdT vol. 11 combined files; notes, rests and other musical events are otherwise unchanged.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-25" resp="#resp.tu">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>Page-level OMR correction against the DdT facsimile: Jingyu Tu corrected the page files for BSB images 00063-00091 in mei-friend from 2026-07-16 to 2026-08-16 and made a second pass over BSB images 00063-00067 on 2026-10-25 (178 commits in all).</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
      </revisionDesc>
   </meiHead>
